│ patch_name               │ server_centric_routing_trees                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The program has been structurally redesigned to use "Server-Centric Routing Trees".       │
│                          │ Instead of running Dijkstra's algorithm on-demand for every source-server pair (which     │
│                          │ scales poorly with many sources), we precompute the shortest path tree from each server   │
│                          │ to all nodes in the graph. This architectural shift reduces the number of Dijkstra        │
│                          │ executions from O(num_sources * num_servers) to O(num_servers), drastically improving     │
│                          │ execution speed. Furthermore, this allows us to evaluate all servers for each task source │
│                          │ in O(1) time using a more accurate multi-objective scoring function that directly models  │
│                          │ transmission latency, routing energy, and M/M/1 queueing delay, rather than relying on    │
│                          │ simple hop-count heuristics.                                                              │
