│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pareto_lagrangian_local_search                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite uses a **two-stage Pareto + local-search optimizer** instead of the original │
│                          │ one-pass greedy assignment.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Candidate generation (multi-objective path discovery):**                             │
│                          │    For each task source, it runs multiple Dijkstra passes with different latency/energy   │
│                          │ tradeoff weights (Lagrangian scalarizations). This produces diverse source→server path    │
│                          │ candidates, then keeps the best non-dominated ones.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Global assignment optimization (load-coupled):**                                     │
│                          │    It initializes a feasible assignment, then performs iterative **best-response local    │
│                          │ search** with incremental load updates. Each move evaluates full system impact:           │
│                          │    - routing latency + routing energy from chosen path,                                   │
│                          │    - server queueing latency using an M/M/1-like delay model,                             │
│                          │    - server compute energy (dynamic + shared idle activation cost).                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach is fundamentally different from the old ranked greedy method because it     │
│                          │ explicitly explores multi-objective path tradeoffs first and then optimizes assignments   │
│                          │ under server-load coupling globally. It tends to perform better when latency/energy       │
│                          │ tradeoffs and queue congestion interact.                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
