│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alt_paths_and_marginal_energy                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main remaining weakness: each source-server pair currently relies   │
│                          │ only on three fixed server-rooted shortest-path trees, which limits path diversity. The   │
│                          │ prior recommendation suggests adding a small number of nearby non-tree alternatives, and  │
│                          │ that is exactly what this change does in a lightweight way.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The update introduces a single additional path variant per promising source-server pair   │
│                          │ using a shortest-path search that penalizes edges from the already selected base path.    │
│                          │ This tends to produce a nearby alternative with similar feasibility but sometimes better  │
│                          │ latency/energy tradeoff under the true objective. Because there are only a few servers,   │
│                          │ this remains computationally manageable.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second refinement improves scoring fidelity: instead of charging the full server      │
│                          │ compute energy after assignment, it uses the marginal compute-energy increase caused by   │
│                          │ assigning the current task to that server. This better matches incremental                │
│                          │ decision-making in greedy/local-search assignment and helps avoid over-penalizing         │
│                          │ already-active servers, which often improves both latency and total energy together.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this is a targeted change: preserve the strong server-precomputation structure,  │
│                          │ enrich candidate diversity with one extra path where it matters, and make assignment      │
│                          │ scoring better aligned with the actual system objective.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0456                                                                                   │
