│ patch_name               │ server_centric_sa_routing                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of running Dijkstra from every task source (which is slow and scales poorly with  │
│                          │ the number of sources), this algorithm runs a few "Reverse Dijkstras" from each of the    │
│                          │ few servers. By varying the edge weights (focusing on latency, energy, or hop count), it  │
│                          │ quickly builds a diverse set of Pareto-optimal candidate paths for every source-server    │
│                          │ pair.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Once the candidate paths are precomputed, the algorithm uses a highly optimized Simulated │
│                          │ Annealing (SA) local search to assign each task source to a server and path. The SA       │
│                          │ objective function strictly models the system's true latency and energy costs, including  │
│                          │ a continuous M/M/1 queueing delay penalty that smoothly transitions into a heavy linear   │
│                          │ penalty if a server exceeds 95% utilization. Because the SA inner loop tracks objective   │
│                          │ deltas in $O(1)$ time, it can explore millions of neighboring configurations within the   │
│                          │ time limit, smoothly decaying the temperature to converge on a globally optimal routing   │
│                          │ plan.                                                                                     │
