│ patch_name               │ server_rooted_multitree_routing                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the simplistic per-(source,server) shortest path and hop-based scoring with a     │
│                          │ server-rooted multi-tree candidate strategy plus load-aware assignment.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Few servers, many sources optimization**: precompute multiple routing trees per      │
│                          │ server (latency/energy blends), instead of running many source-target shortest paths      │
│                          │ repeatedly.                                                                               │
│                          │ 2. **Candidate diversity**: for each server, build 4 alternative trees with different     │
│                          │ latency-energy-capacity weightings to expose better Pareto tradeoffs.                     │
│                          │ 3. **Accurate path evaluation**: compute actual route latency and route energy per source │
│                          │ using its payload on the chosen path.                                                     │
│                          │ 4. **Queue-aware greedy assignment**: assign larger workloads first with explicit         │
│                          │ queue-delay and compute-energy terms, respecting stability.                               │
│                          │ 5. **Light local refinement**: one improvement pass to reassign heavy tasks when          │
│                          │ beneficial.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly addresses the observed weakness (high latency + energy from simplistic      │
│                          │ scoring and single-path style) while keeping runtime practical.                           │
