│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ server_diverse_multicriteria_routing                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite changes the program from repeated per-source shortest-path searches into a   │
│                          │ server-centric, modular planning pipeline.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Structural changes:                                                                       │
│                          │ - Precompute multi-criteria shortest-path trees from each server using several            │
│                          │ latency/energy tradeoff weights, instead of recomputing one path per source-server pair.  │
│                          │ - Build server-diverse candidate sets for each source first, keeping the best path        │
│                          │ variants per server before global pruning. This prevents one server from dominating the   │
│                          │ candidate pool and improves assignment quality.                                           │
│                          │ - Separate the logic into clear phases: graph building, path-tree generation, candidate   │
│                          │ extraction, greedy assignment, and local improvement.                                     │
│                          │ - Use a more faithful objective proxy combining transmission latency, routing energy,     │
│                          │ queueing delay, and compute energy with the task’s actual payload and compute demand.     │
│                          │ - Add a lightweight local reassignment pass after greedy construction to reduce score     │
│                          │ further without expensive global search.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This organization improves maintainability and runtime efficiency on graphs with few      │
│                          │ servers and many task sources, while usually producing better latency-energy tradeoffs.   │
