╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ capacity_regret_router                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite changes the solver from a simple source-by-source greedy assignment into a   │
│                          │ modular two-stage architecture:                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Candidate generation layer**:                                                        │
│                          │    - Builds a compact set of path candidates per `(source, server)` using several         │
│                          │ server-rooted shortest-path trees with different latency/energy trade-offs.               │
│                          │    - Separates path extraction and metric computation cleanly.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Capacity-aware assignment layer**:                                                   │
│                          │    - Uses **feasibility-weighted regret ordering** instead of only heavy-task ordering.   │
│                          │    - For each unassigned source, it compares the best and second-best marginal            │
│                          │ placements, but also boosts priority for sources that have few safe server options under  │
│                          │ soft/hard utilization limits.                                                             │
│                          │    - This better preserves scarce low-cost server capacity for hard-to-place tasks.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Improvement layer**:                                                                 │
│                          │    - Runs multiple local improvement passes with remove-and-reinsert evaluation.          │
│                          │    - Reconsiders both server choice and route choice under updated loads.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The redesign improves maintainability by explicitly separating graph preprocessing,       │
│                          │ candidate generation, marginal scoring, regret scheduling, and local search. It also      │
│                          │ improves optimization quality by making assignment decisions more load-sensitive and      │
│                          │ capacity-aware, which should reduce queueing latency without overusing expensive routing  │
│                          │ or server energy.                                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0703                                                                                   │
