│ patch_description        │ This implementation optimizes task routing using a marginal cost approach. It precomputes │
│                          │ shortest path trees from each server to all potential source nodes using a balanced       │
│                          │ weight of latency and routing energy. Task sources are then assigned by calculating the   │
│                          │ marginal increase in total system latency (including queueing externalities for existing  │
│                          │ tasks) and system energy. This combined crossover balances the greedy packing of the      │
│                          │ first implementation with the precise marginal cost analysis of the second, adding a      │
│                          │ quadratic utilization penalty to prevent server saturation near the capacity limit.       │
