│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ marginal_objective_routing                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Aligns the greedy assignment and local search scoring with the true marginal              │
│                          │ contributions to the global sum of latencies and total system energy.                     │
│                          │ 1. **Marginal Queueing Delay**: Uses the exact marginal increase in the total number of   │
│                          │ tasks in the server (`new_load / (service_rate - new_load) - old_load / (service_rate -   │
│                          │ old_load)`) to perfectly represent the marginal increase in the total system latency.     │
│                          │ 2. **Marginal Compute Energy**: Calculates the marginal dynamic energy difference when    │
│                          │ adding a task.                                                                            │
│                          │ 3. **Enhanced Candidate Diversity**: Increases the number of precomputed routing modes    │
│                          │ from 3 to 6 per server, exploring more diverse blends of latency, energy, and capacity    │
│                          │ penalties.                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. **Multi-pass Local Improvement**: Increases the local improvement passes from 1 to 2   │
│                          │ and adds a tiny "stickiness" bonus to the exact same path to prevent unnecessary flapping │
│                          │ while allowing the system to settle into a deeper local optimum.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
