│ patch_description        │ This rewrite keeps the same interface and output format, but changes the internal         │
│                          │ assignment strategy to be more capacity-aware and more consistent with the two-objective  │
│                          │ goal.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main changes:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Precompute multiple shortest-path trees per server using several latency/energy         │
│                          │ scalarizations, then keep the best path variants.                                         │
│                          │ - Build per-source server candidates with explicit routing latency, routing energy, and   │
│                          │ compute-energy estimates.                                                                 │
│                          │ - Use feasibility-weighted regret ordering: sources with few safe server options and high │
│                          │ regret are assigned earlier, which helps preserve scarce low-cost server capacity for     │
│                          │ hard-to-place tasks.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Use a stronger incremental scoring model that jointly considers transmission latency,   │
│                          │ queueing delay, routing energy, compute energy, and utilization penalties.                │
│                          │ - Apply local improvement passes with relocation and limited pairwise swap search to      │
│                          │ reduce the global proxy objective after the initial greedy construction.                  │
│                          │ - Preserve valid simple paths and include defensive repair logic.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation is still lightweight enough for the grading timeout, but should        │
│                          │ improve assignment calibration versus the previous purely best-cost greedy behavior.      │
