│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ two_candidate_server_trees_incremental_scoring                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This edit introduces a bounded path-diversity strategy plus a stronger assignment         │
│                          │ objective.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1) **Up to 2 precomputed path candidates per server**                                     │
│                          │ For each server, we run two server-rooted Dijkstra trees with different latency/energy    │
│                          │ route weights. This cheaply creates alternate source→server paths that can trade off      │
│                          │ transmission latency vs routing energy. We keep the second tree only if it is             │
│                          │ structurally different (different parent map on reachable nodes), avoiding redundant      │
│                          │ work.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2) **Incremental queue-aware assignment scoring**                                         │
│                          │ The assignment objective is changed from a static per-source score to a marginal          │
│                          │ system-impact score:                                                                      │
│                          │ - latency term includes transmission + queueing, plus queue externality on already        │
│                          │ assigned arrivals at that server,                                                         │
│                          │ - energy term includes routing + dynamic compute + first-use idle activation cost         │
│                          │ (discounted),                                                                             │
│                          │ - a light utilization regularizer discourages near-saturation choices.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3) **Path reconstruction robustness**                                                     │
│                          │ Selected `(server, candidate_tree)` is tracked and reconstructed with loop/length         │
│                          │ safeguards to keep valid simple paths.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This remains efficient (few servers, many sources) while exploring a small but useful     │
│                          │ route set per server.                                                                     │
