│ patch_description        │ We introduce a fourth, highly capacity-aware routing mode dynamically via `run_dijkstra`  │
│                          │ which uses a heavier weight (`gamma = 5.0`) on the inverse capacity term. Since task      │
│                          │ sources often face bottlenecks dependent on their specific edge capacity limits           │
│                          │ (especially high-payload ones), this explores a new structural alternative.               │
│                          │ To prevent an explosion of options and to only keep this alternative when it represents   │
│                          │ an objectively beneficial route for the specific payload, we filter candidates at the     │
│                          │ source-server level taking only Pareto front solutions (considering specific              │
│                          │ `payload`-adjusted `p_lat` and `p_ene`). This strictly improves the tightness of our      │
│                          │ route options.                                                                            │
