│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dynamic_regret_active_pool                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a dynamic regret active-pool constructor for assignment order.                  │
│                          │ Instead of committing directly to the single highest-priority source each step, we now:   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Recompute regret with current server loads (still fully dynamic).                      │
│                          │ 2. Build a small active pool of highest-regret sources.                                   │
│                          │ 3. Choose the source within that pool whose best feasible assignment has the lowest       │
│                          │ immediate marginal delta.                                                                 │
│                          │ 4. Keep a regret-aware fallback if feasibility is tight.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the beneficial regret signal (protecting constrained tasks) while reducing     │
│                          │ greedy over-commitment that can hurt latency/energy later due to queue buildup. I also    │
│                          │ slightly adjust the priority formula to avoid favoring high primary cost too              │
│                          │ aggressively.                                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
