│                          │ each server, we generate 3 trees using different latency/energy/capacity blends. When     │
│                          │ reconstructing paths for a source, we evaluate them and keep only the best path           │
│                          │ (minimizing a combined metric) plus at most one alternate path that offers a materially   │
│                          │ different tradeoff (e.g., >5% lower latency or energy). This ensures a compact, diverse   │
│                          │ candidate set. The assignment phase uses a mathematically exact marginal cost formulation │
│                          │ for both latency (queueing delay derivative) and energy, followed by a regret-based       │
│                          │ greedy initialization and local search refinement.                                        │
