│ patch_description        │ This approach replaces generic shortest-path edge scaling with theoretically sound path   │
│                          │ weights centered on average payload, perfectly aligning the Dijkstra path selection with  │
│                          │ the network objective. Next, we replace the single-pass broad local search with an        │
│                          │ Iterative Best Response (IBR) load management algorithm. By using mathematically precise  │
│                          │ surrogate derivatives for both queue delay and system energy, we assign initial server    │
│                          │ allocations and iteratively target explicitly "hot" (highly stressed) servers.            │
│                          │ Unburdening the worst localized bottlenecks monotonically pushes the system globally into │
│                          │ a highly balanced Pareto-optimal local minimum efficiently over multiple targeted         │
│                          │ relaxation passes, including a bounded pairwise swap phase to escape strict capacity      │
│                          │ limits.                                                                                   │
