│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dynamic_regret_active_pool                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the one-shot static regret ordering with a tiny dynamic-regret active-pool        │
│                          │ scheduler.                                                                                │
│                          │ Instead of computing regret only once at zero load, this recomputes best/second-best      │
│                          │ choices for a small pool of currently unassigned tasks under current server loads, then   │
│                          │ assigns the highest-regret task next.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Static regret gets stale quickly as server queues fill.                                 │
│                          │ - Dynamic regret better protects “fragile” tasks (few feasible low-cost options),         │
│                          │ reducing late overload and queue spikes.                                                  │
│                          │ - Active-pool limits runtime overhead versus full global recomputation.                   │
│                          │ - A mild scarcity term improves feasibility and stabilizes both latency and energy.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a targeted edit in the assignment layer only; path validity and fallback behavior │
│                          │ remain robust.                                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
